                                "text": "The present writer was once asked to name what he considered to be \"the most typically English railway approach to a town\": a somewhat tall order, especially as such matters will always be, in the last resort, of individual opinion. But the unhesitating answer to this question (which has not been altered after many years of extended travel throughout England) was \"Sudbury, in Suffolk.\""
